.TH LIBWEACT 3 "October 2026" "WeAct35 1.0.0" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
libweact \- C graphics, transport and guarded FS35 library
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <weact/weact_extended.h>
#include <weact/weact_graphics.h>
cc app.c $(pkg-config --cflags --libs weact) -o app
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
libweact.so.1 provides legacy FS096 framebuffer functions and additive wx_*
surfaces, devices, protocol encoders, transports and managed FS35 setup.
Install libweact-dev for headers, static library and weact.pc.  The 1.0.0 ABI
has SONAME libweact.so.1 and 79 exports.
.PP
New code normally creates an explicit wx_surface_t or wx_device_t with an
explicit model and pixel format.  WX_FS096 is 160 by 80 legacy BRG565/MSB;
WX_FS35 is 480 by 320 RGB565 little-endian in landscape.  A surface is host
memory.  wx_device_bitmap sends its full canvas; wx_device_bitmap_region sends
a strict canvas rectangle.
.SH LIFECYCLE AND ERRORS
Factory objects returned through out parameters are caller-owned: destroy
surfaces with wx_surface_destroy, devices with wx_device_destroy, and POSIX
transport with wx_posix_transport_destroy.  Borrowed canvas/pixel pointers are
not freed by callers.  wx_status_t reports API failures.  Managed FS35 setup
reports detailed stage/reason/errno in wx_init_report_t.
.PP
wx_posix_init_connector_select creates the guarded FS35 connector.  Then
wx_device_init performs orientation 02 confirmation and black full Fill;
wx_device_init_preserve followed by wx_device_confirm_orientation avoids a
setter/Fill and accepts confirmed landscape 02 or 03.  Failed transfers seal
the stream: do not retry a partial command or automatically reconnect.
.SH HARDWARE SAFETY
Both models share VID:PID 1a86:fe0c.  Verify exact Product, stable by-id path,
permissions and port ownership.  The low-level POSIX transport itself does not
perform these guards; use the managed guarded connector where appropriate.
.SH COMPATIBILITY
The legacy public weact_display_t ABI remains available.  Use its BRG565
functions only for its legacy profile.  QR/barcode planning and CLI syntax are
not a public libweact C API.
.SH SEE ALSO
The complete function, type and ownership reference is installed/source
documentation API.md.  See also
.BR weact-cli (1),
.BR weactterm (1)
